{
  "$comment": "Where the post and comment boxes are, per site, so the sign control can sit beside them. This list places the control and nothing else: nothing in verification, canonicalisation, URL handling or the site derivation reads it, and a site with no entry still signs from the toolbar popup or the context menu. `site` is the registrable domain (mail.google.com is google.com), `selectors` are CSS selectors of the editable boxes, in the light DOM (a box inside a closed shadow root cannot be reached), and `binding` is `page` unless the site is a chat service with a stable URL per channel. Selectors rot whenever a site redesigns, so this list is maintained by everyone: add or fix an entry with a pull request, and say in it which page you checked and when. Entries are wanted for every site people write on, in every country; the README lists the ones we know we are missing.",
  "sites": [
    {
      "site": "x.com",
      "name": "X",
      "selectors": [
        "div[data-testid='tweetTextarea_0']",
        "div[data-testid^='tweetTextarea_']"
      ],
      "binding": "page"
    },
    {
